(423723, 37445, 7969, '<td valign="top">My shot was representing, to me, that the militaristic voice of freedom should be restrained. I was not condoning freedom at the cost of human life.  I am not at all in favor of war as a solution to the difficulties life presents, surely IMO there are more civilized ways to solve problems.  Thanks to those of you who commented, sorry for the confusion, though I am glad my shot made folks think some  :  ).<br/>lynn<br/> <br/>BTW it was NOT shot in sepia, this is straight out of camera with slight crop. Was a rainy day and this was the colors camera picked up.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-09-19 00:18:25.</i></td>', 'My shot was representing, to me, that the militaristic voice of freedom should be restrained. I was not condoning freedom at the cost of human life.  I am not at all in favor of war as a solution to the difficulties life presents, surely IMO there are more civilized ways to solve problems.  Thanks to those of you who commented, sorry for the confusion, though I am glad my shot made folks think some  :  ).lynn BTW it was NOT shot in sepia, this is straight out of camera with slight crop. Was a rainy day and this was the colors camera picked up.', '2003-09-19 01:06:01.000000', '2003-09-19 01:18:25.000000', 0),
(423731, 37435, 10643, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry that my score suffered for the glare from the plastic book jackets. I didn''t take them off because I wanted it to be 100% clear that these are library books. You can go to the free public library anywhere and get books that not so long ago you may not have been allowed to read. Many are ones that kids in many schools across the country are still not allowed to read. That''s the real freedom I was communicating here. The button was purchased at a bookstore in Denver, but it is available from <a href="//www.asja.org/store/button.php" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.asja.org/store/button.php</a> for only a dollar.</td>', 'I''m sorry that my score suffered for the glare from the plastic book jackets. I didn''t take them off because I wanted it to be 100% clear that these are library books. You can go to the free public library anywhere and get books that not so long ago you may not have been allowed to read. Many are ones that kids in many schools across the country are still not allowed to read. That''s the real freedom I was communicating here. The button was purchased at a bookstore in Denver, but it is available from //www.asja.org/store/button.php for only a dollar.', '2003-09-19 01:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
